lesson: 79
title: A number we do not need
stars: 1
explain: Some stories tell us a number that the question does not ask about. Find what the question asks, and use only the numbers that belong to it.
explain: «Max has 15 cards and 7 marbles. He gives 4 cards to Zoe. How many cards does he have left?» The 7 marbles do not matter: 15 - 4 = 11 cards.
explain: Before you add or subtract, say in words what each number counts.
vars: a=name b=name c=name t=thing n=8..90 m=2..60 e=2..50 y=6..11
need: n - m >= 2
need: e != n && e != m
answer: n - m
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}. {a.He} gives {m} {t} to {b}, who already has {e}. How many {t} does {a} have now?
exercise: {a} is {y} years old. {a.He} had {n} {t} and lost {m} of them. How many {t} does {a.he} have left?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}, {b} has {m} {t} and {c} has {e} {t}. How many more {t} does {a} have than {b}?
exercise: A shop had {n} {t} and {e} bags. It sold {m} {t}. How many {t} are left in the shop?
exercise: {a} had {m} {t}. {b} gave {a.him} some more, and now {a} has {n}. {c} has {e} {t}. How many {t} did {b} give {a}?
exercise: There are {n} {t} on a table and {e} chairs around it. {a} takes {m} {t}. How many {t} are still on the table?
test: {e} children are in {a}'s class. {a} brought {n} {t} to school and handed out {m}. How many {t} has {a.he} still got?
test: {c}, who has {e} {t}, watches {a} and {b}. {a} owns {n} {t} and {b} owns {m}. By how many {t} does {a} beat {b}?
test: It took {a} {e} minutes to find {m} more {t}, and now {a.he} has {n}. How many {t} did {a.he} have before?
test: At the fair, {a} sold {m} of {a.his} {n} {t} for {e} dollars. How many {t} did {a.he} keep?
test: {a} counts {n} {t}; {b} counts {m} {t} and {e} stamps. How many fewer {t} does {b} count?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t} and {e} toy cars. {a.He} hands out {m} {t}. How many {t} does {a} have left?
exercise: {a} lives in Ohio and is {y} years old. {a.He} had {n} {t} and gave away {m}. How many {t} remain?
exercise: A shop in Dublin had {n} {t} and {e} toy cars. It sold {m} {t}. How many {t} does the shop still have?
exercise: {a} had {n} {t}. {a.He} donated {m} of them to a school {e} km away. How many {t} does {a} still have?
exercise: {b} has {m} {t} and {e} toy cars; {a} has {n} {t}. How many fewer {t} does {b} have than {a}?
exercise: In {y} minutes, {a} sold {m} of {a.his} {n} {t} at a market in Kent. How many {t} were not sold?
exercise: {a} had {m} {t}. After a trip to Canada that took {e} days, {a.he} had {n} {t}. How many {t} did {a.he} gain on the trip?
exercise: There were {n} {t} in a box and {e} pens beside it. {a} took out {m} {t}. How many {t} were left in the box?
test: {c} is {y} years old. {a} owns {n} {t}, and {b} owns {m}. How many more {t} does {a} own than {b}?
test: A bakery in Sydney baked {n} rolls and {e} pies. By noon {m} rolls were sold. How many rolls had not been sold?
test: {a} rode {e} km to a fair in Alberta with {n} {t} and came home with {m.words} fewer. How many {t} did {a.he} bring home?
test: How many {t} are still in the jar if {a} took {m} of the {n} {t} in it, and {b} took {e} rulers from the desk?
test: {a} has {n} {t}; {b}, who is {y}, has {m} {t}. By how many {t} does {b} trail {a}?
test: After {b} gave {a} some {t}, {a} had {n}. Before that, {a} had {m}, and {c} had {e}. How many {t} did {b} give?
