exam: Whereas {a} held {n} {t} and transferred {m} of them to {b}, who previously held {e}, determine the quantity hereinafter retained by {a}.
exam: It is given that {a}, aged {y} years, possessed {n} {t} and subsequently mislaid {m} thereof. Ascertain the number of {t} remaining in {a.his} possession.
exam: A receptacle bearing the number {e} contained {n} {t}, of which {m} were removed. State the number of {t} remaining therein.
exam: Disregarding the fact that {c} holds {e} {t}, compute the residual holding of {a}, whose stock of {n} {t} was diminished by {m}.
exercise: The farm had {n} sheep and {e} cows. In the cold snap, {m} of the sheep didn't make it. How many sheep are left?
exercise: {a}'s mum earned {n} dollars a week until she was let go. Her new job, {e} km away, pays {m} dollars less a week. How many dollars a week does she earn now?
test: nan's {e+60} and 'a bit forgetful' — had {n} {t}, gave {m} to {b} and forgot all about it. how many's she got left, honestly
